  Two things worth your eye when you read it, both places where I made a call you might not:

  - [1m[38;5;153mlogin()[39m calls [38;5;153mtrackEvent[39m itself[0m rather than the submit handler doing it. It means [38;5;153mlogin[39m does two things now. I chose
    it because [38;5;153mlogin()[39m is the only place that knows the auth outcome, and a caller that forgets to track fails
    silently.
  - [1m[38;5;153mapp.js[39m needs a [38;5;153mtypeof document !== "undefined"[39m guard[0m around its DOM wiring. That's a direct consequence of wanting
    [38;5;153mnode:test[39m unit tests — without it, requiring [38;5;153mapp.js[39m under Node crashes on [38;5;153mdocument.getElementById[39m. It's a small wart
    on the browser file that exists purely to serve testability.

